# Copy to .env.local and fill in as needed. .env* is git-ignored; never commit
# real values. Both variables are read server-side only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix) -- neither is ever shipped to the browser bundle.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the Next.js server-side proxy route (src/app/api/[...path]/route.ts)
# forwards API requests to. Defaults to http://localhost:8000 if unset, which
# is right for local dev against the backend started per docs/../startup.md.
#
# In docker-compose.offline.yml this is set to http://backend:8000 (the
# service name on the internal network), not read from this file.
#
# On Vercel or another host, point this at the backend's reachable URL, e.g.:
# API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixtures (dev only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to serve every read from the two demo assessments in
# src/lib/fixtures/ instead of the backend, so the whole dashboard renders
# with no backend running at all. Leave unset in any deployed environment.
# USE_FIXTURES=1
